  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 137 PM EDT Thu Jul 30 2026\n\n- Rain Chances Return Friday Night into Saturday\n\nDry conditions continue through most of Friday, but an advancing \nmid level trough and surface low will move in Friday night into \nSaturday. There is a 20 percent chance of an isolated shower \nbefore 8pm, otherwise chances increase to around 70 to 80 percent \nby Saturday morning. There is the potential (20 percent) for \nthunder with the rain into Saturday. Overall probabilities are \nhigher that amounts will remain under an inch, however there is a \n30 to 40 percent chance of amounts over an inch across the area, \nwith an isolated 20 percent chance of greater than 2 inches \nthrough Saturday. WPC currently has the area in a marginal risk \nfor excessive rainfall Friday night into early Saturday morning. \nIf we see more low to mid level support with the low pressure \nsystem tracking to the south, higher rainfall amounts will be \npossible and may cause some minor flooding. Showers slowly clear \nSaturday night into Sunday morning with dry conditions expected \nthrough Tuesday.\n\n- Additional Rain Chances Tuesday Night into Wednesday\n\nPressure heights fall again with another shortwave trough moving \nthrough midweek next week. Overall the wave is rather open and \nshallow, therefore not expecting any significant rainfall or \nthunderstorm potential. Probabilities for rain are 20 to 30 \npercent with the best chances for any thunder Wednesday afternoon.",
